        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: поражение",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "поражение (porazhéniye) — \"a defeat\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "После поражения игроки долго молчали. Pósle porazhéniya igrokí dólgo molcháli. After the defeat the players were silent for a long time."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Neuter. Потерпеть поражение (porazhéniye) — to suffer a defeat."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "поражение (porazhéniye) is built on поразить 'to strike, to defeat', from разить 'to strike'; EtymDB lists it, glossed 'defeat', without a source."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for telling, explaining and describing at B1."
